I need to implement timeline feature:
TimelineLib
  consists of a list of events and event archtypes (listed in two separate data files)
  Example of event_archtype:
  credits_or_deterioration{
    options:[ //list of Rewards
      reward that takes away 100 credits
      reward which causes deterioration of a random available raid //needs to be implemented
    ]
    icon: { kind: 'itemImage', key: 'cyan', scale: 1, offset: { x: 0, y: 0 } },
  }
  Example of list of events
  events:[
    {
      type:credits_or_deterioration
      time:[1, 10, 40] //when event accurs - day, hour, minute. needs to be parsed into a float
      repeat:[4, 0, 0] //how often does it repeat
    }
    ]

GameState has a list of timeline events. all events from the list are placed there is a sorted order. repeated events are only placed once. Whenever time advances it checks if an event is due and teh event is executed. If it is a repeated events - its next installment is added to the timeline

executing event:
the player can choose what happens - which of the Rewards from the options is going to fire. By default the [0] item is chosen. The user choice will be implemented separately, later in UI. If the player doesn't have enough resources, then the next is choosen.

Executed events stay in the timeline. gameState keeps a cursor into it.

Before coding, let's discuss it and iron out what is underspecified.